==English==

===Etymology===
From the character [[w:Caspar Milquetoast|Caspar Milquetoast]] of the comic strip ''The Timid Soul'', created by Harold Webster and first published in 1924 (named after the American dish [[w:Milk toast|milk toast]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪlktəʊst/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[meek|Meek]], [[timid]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|pejorative}} A [[person]] of [[meek]] or [[timid]] [[disposition]].

